y not believe what I found and just how bad this gets. \n\nOut soon at https://t.co/0iAdu05vHj.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 264}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVHSnf9B", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8832805, "raw_content": "Stop blaming Israel, that's what they are there for. Israel is Our Mess, it's a deflection.\n", "author": "Mega_MAGA", "created": 1789309092607, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Mega_MAGA", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Israel is Our Deep State, Wake Up.", "last_comment_created": 1789323934572, "content": "<p>Stop blaming Israel, that's what they are there for. Israel is Our Mess, it's a deflection.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up": 23, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVHSnwau", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 16, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8832960, "raw_content": "", "author": "VanillaCupCake", "created": 1789316142397, "profile_picture": "skHhaQnk6Zfk", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Beelzy", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVHSnwau.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/Y4pPwsVUvUg8.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/JfTmP37fXmyA9l9y.jpeg", "width": 768, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 686}], "blurhash": "UQC?M]ofaKWBogayoffQ~XjZofof%2oLWBWB", "full_resolution": [849, 951]}, "title": "LOL", "last_comment_created": 1789317136478, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 1, "score_up": 16, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVHSnfHT", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 22, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8832827, "raw_content": "https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/aug/25/china-dismisses-us-sanctions-iran-says-not-submit-economic-warfare/\n\n\u201cEconomic warfare and maximum pressure provide no solution. On the contrary, they only serve to fuel tensions and lead to risk spillover, which will disrupt the global economic and financial order, and harm the legitimate rights and interests of other countries,\u201d Mr. Lin said. \u201cChina\u2019s cooperation with Iran is conducted within the framework of international law, thus should not be disrupted. China is closely following the developments, and will do everything necessary to firmly safeguard its rights and interests.\u201d\n\nChina remains one of Iran\u2019s most valuable links to international markets. Beijing purchases about 90% of Iran\u2019s crude oil, and Tehran maintains access to China\u2019s banking system, which helps Iran mitigate the effects of Western sanctions.\n\nThe Treasury Department designated more than 60 entities and ordered Bank Melli Iran to shut down, but Chinese state banks were largely spared.\n\nIf U.S. sanctions hit Chinese banks hard and cut them off from the U.S. dollar system, it could undermine the dollar\u2019s centrality in global trade and, in turn, the power of Western sanctions.\n\nEmily Kilcrease, senior director of the Energy, Economics and Security Program at the Center for a New American Security, said removing Chinese banks from the U.S. dollar system is the \u201cnuclear option.\u201d\n\n\u201cThey are the largest banks in the world and they facilitate China\u2019s trade with the world,\u201d Ms. Kilcrease told The Washington Times. \u201cAnd so you have to keep in mind that if you sanction one of those Chinese banks, you\u2019re going to have a damaging effect on overall global financial stability by taking out one of the major institutions in a very disruptive, abrupt way.\u201d", "author": "OrangeManNotBad", "created": 1789309867036, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "China indicated Tuesday that it would not adhere to demands from the Treasury Department to cut off all economic ties to Iran, citing risks to international stability and asserting it would not bow to \u201ceconomic warfare.\u201d", "last_comment_created": 1789309867036, "content": "<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/aug/25/china-dismisses-us-sanctions-iran-says-not-submit-economic-warfare/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/aug/25/china-dismisses-us-sanctions-iran-says-not-submit-economic-warfare/</a></p>\n<p>\u201cEconomic warfare and maximum pressure provide no solution. On the contrary, they only serve to fuel tensions and lead to risk spillover, which will disrupt the global economic and financial order, and harm the legitimate rights and interests of other countries,\u201d Mr. Lin said. \u201cChina\u2019s cooperation with Iran is conducted within the framework of international law, thus should not be disrupted. China is closely following the developments, and will do everything necessary to firmly safeguard its rights and interests.\u201d</p>\n<p>China remains one of Iran\u2019s most valuable links to international markets. Beijing purchases about 90% of Iran\u2019s crude oil, and Tehran maintains access to China\u2019s banking system, which helps Iran mitigate the effects of Western sanctions.</p>\n<p>The Treasury Department designated more than 60 entities and ordered Bank Melli Iran to shut down, but Chinese state banks were largely spared.</p>\n<p>If U.S. sanctions hit Chinese banks hard and cut them off from the U.S. dollar system, it could undermine the dollar\u2019s centrality in global trade and, in turn, the power of Western sanctions.</p>\n<p>Emily Kilcrease, senior director of the Energy, Economics and Security Program at the Center for a New American Security, said removing Chinese banks from the U.S. dollar system is the \u201cnuclear option.\u201d</p>\n<p>\u201cThey are the largest banks in the world and they facilitate China\u2019s trade with the world,\u201d Ms. Kilcrease told The Washington Times. \u201cAnd so you have to keep in mind that if you sanction one of those Chinese banks, you\u2019re going to have a damaging effect on overall global financial stability by taking out one of the major institutions in a very disruptive, abrupt way.\u201d</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 22, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_fl